**1. A bearing structure comprising:**

a housing having a bearing hole extending along an axis;

a bearing disposed in the bearing hole and configured to rotatably support a shaft about the axis;

an oil drainage passage formed in a lower portion of the housing; and

a clearance groove formed in an inner peripheral surface of the bearing hole, the clearance groove communicating with the oil drainage passage and defining a circumferentially asymmetric gap between the housing and the bearing,

wherein, relative to a predetermined rotation direction of the shaft, the gap has a first radial dimension on a downstream side of the clearance groove and a second radial dimension on an upstream side of the clearance groove, the first radial dimension being greater than the second radial dimension.
